<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-034-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Ch. XV: eggs as solids of revolution of a definite, species-varying family of ovoid meridian curves (Preston 1953 family on Biggins et al. 2018 / Deeming 2018 data) — Code-to-model traceability: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The module header maps each section to Thompson's pages (652, 654, 655, 657-659) and to the five Lean theorems (L1-57); function docstrings cite Biggins Analysis.R (estimator, fat.point), Lean law numbers and Thompson page numbers; the Math KG YAML links each law to code loci and Lean loci (alignment and integrity gates pass)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-034-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-034-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-034-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Ch. XV: eggs as solids of revolution of a definite, species-varying family of ovoid meridian curves (Preston 1953 family on Biggins et al. 2018 / Deeming 2018 data) — Model fidelity to source: 91/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Implements the Preston family, indices and exact volume (L110-184) matching Lean Laws 1-2, and now exercises Thompson's own mechanics: the envelope equation inverted as 2H(x) = (P - p_n)/T with exact pole limits (L186-210), the four-constraint Thompson closure that recovers C126 and the sphere (L212-246), the empirical pressure-asymmetry path (L248-277) and the cone-balance ratio (L279-286), all cross-referenced to the 5 Lean theorems. The closure is kinematic (curvature <-> pressure) rather than a dynamic oviduct model with friction, which Thompson himself invokes." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "thompson/claims/t1917-034_on-the-shapes-of-eggs-and-of-certain-other-hollo.py L248–L277: Pressure path is a conditional-mean regression through the data, not a solved membrane dynamics problem <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/2514d4650/thompson/claims/t1917-034_on-the-shapes-of-eggs-and-of-certain-other-hollo.py#L248-L277>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-034-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-034-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-034-model-fidelity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.1e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-034-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Ch. XV: eggs as solids of revolution of a definite, species-varying family of ovoid meridian curves (Preston 1953 family on Biggins et al. 2018 / Deeming 2018 data) — Morphometric validation: 92/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L816-871) returns 17 reference-anchored measurements: min elongation 1.035 (ref 1), axisymmetry 0.048 mean (ref 0), C126 photo E 1.8616 vs 1.8607 and PA 2.67 vs 2.63, profile r = 0.99999, Preston RMSE/B 0.0023 on C126 vs 0.0018 median, Cartesian oval 0.0172 (7.4x) and ellipsoid 0.0731 (31x) negative controls, Baker ratio 35x, eta^2 0.67 (p = 2e-100), order eta^2 0.38 / 0.57, KS D = 0.96 (p = 1e-135), class ordering, Spearman rho 0.39 (p = 7e-8), closure residual 5.6e-16, pressure-path r = 0.54 and CV of the pressure profile 0.32." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-034-measurement-axisymmetry-residual-rms-upper-lower-profile-half-breadth-mean-over-segmented-eggs>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-034-measurement-baker-2002-2-parameter-alternative-median-mse-ratio-vs-preston-132-eggs>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-034-measurement-between-species-eta-2-of-elongation-30-species>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-034-measurement-c126-elongation-from-photograph-segmentation-vs-published>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-034-measurement-c126-meridian-profile-pearson-r-segmented-fit-vs-published-fit>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-034-measurement-c126-polar-asymmetry-from-photograph-vs-published>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-034-measurement-ks-statistic-uria-aalge-vs-penguin-elongation-distributions>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-034-measurement-mean-cv-of-the-p-p-n-t-profile-over-biggins-eggs-pressure-non-uniformity-sphere-0>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-034-measurement-minimum-elongation-l-b-over-all-eggs-incl-segmented-specimens-prolate-never-oblate>,
